    prov:value "{\"prompt\": null, \"messages\": [{\"role\": \"system\", \"content\": \"Your input fields are:\\n1. `city` (str): \\n2. `weather` (str): \\n3. `facts` (str): \\n4. `note` (str): \\n5. `feedback` (str):\\nYour output fields are:\\n1. `brief` (str):\\nAll interactions will be structured in the following way, with the appropriate values filled in.\\n\\n[[ ## city ## ]]\\n{city}\\n\\n[[ ## weather ## ]]\\n{weather}\\n\\n[[ ## facts ## ]]\\n{facts}\\n\\n[[ ## note ## ]]\\n{note}\\n\\n[[ ## feedback ## ]]\\n{feedback}\\n\\n[[ ## brief ## ]]\\n{brief}\\n\\n[[ ## completed ## ]]\\nIn adhering to this structure, your objective is: \\n        Given the fields `city`, `weather`, `facts`, `note`, `feedback`, produce the fields `brief`.\"}, {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"[[ ## city ## ]]\\nLisbon\\n\\n[[ ## weather ## ]]\\nThe current weather in Lisbon is 21°C with a clear sky.\\n\\n[[ ## facts ## ]]\\nLisbon is the capital of Portugal and is located on the Tagus estuary.\\n\\n[[ ## note ## ]]\\nLisbon is the capital of Portugal and is located on the Tagus estuary.\\n\\n[[ ## feedback ## ]]\\nThe last draft failed review: the first draft is always sent back for revision. Fix it.\\n\\nRespond with the corresponding output fields, starting with the field `[[ ## brief ## ]]`, and then ending with the marker for `[[ ## completed ## ]]`.\"}], \"kwargs\": {}}" ;
